      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>It's not just mistakes though. It's who I am. It's like I'm fundamentally broken in a way that they can't fix. Every time they look at me with that kind of pity or disappointment, it just proves it. I can see the weight of my existence on my parents' faces. I feel like the more I try to be \"better,\" the more I just drag them down with me.",
